  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Transportation obligated $11.3B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department awarded 13,110 contracts with an average award size of $864K. Obligations rose up 25.6% year over year. Annual obligations have trended from $7B in FY21 to $11.3B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $8B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $8.6B in FY24, and $9B in FY25. Engineering Services is the largest procurement category in FY2026 to date with $1.7B in obligations. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing accounted for $1.1B. Telecommunications Resellers accounted for $1B. Other notable categories include Highway, Street, and Bridge Construction with $769M and Computer Systems Design Services with $692M. HARRIS CORPORATION is the largest vendor in FY2026 to date with $1B in obligations. RAYTHEON COMPANY and ROHDE & SCHWARZ USA, INC. follow with $673M and $403M respectively.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the size and recent trend of DOT contract spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Transportation obligated $11.3B in FY2026 to date. Obligations rose up 25.6% year over year. Annual obligations increased from $7B in FY21 to $11.3B in FY26, with intermediate totals of $8B in FY22, $8.7B in FY23, $8.6B in FY24, and $9B in FY25. The Department awarded 13,110 contracts with an average award size of $864K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors receive the most obligations?",
        "body": "Engineering Services received $1.7B in FY2026 to date, making it the largest category. Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing received $1.1B, and Telecommunications Resellers received $1B. HARRIS CORPORATION received $1B in obligations and RAYTHEON COMPANY received $673M; ROHDE & SCHWARZ USA, INC. received $403M."
      }
